#: includes/classes/admin/settings/gpls_woo_rfq_settings.php:822
msgid ""
"<p>In the Normal Checkout mode, a default page called <i>Quote Request</i> "
"is created to view the quote list. This page\n"
"                                            is only needed if in the Normal "
"Checkout mode. (In RFQ mode, the WooCommerce cart\n"
"                                           is used to display the items "
"requested for quote.)</p>\n"
"                                           <p><b>Exclude this page from page "
"caching. \n"
"                                           You can read more <a href=\"https:"
"//neahplugins.com/how-to-make-the-np-quote-plugin-work-with-page-caching/\" "
"target=\"_blank\" >How to make the NP Quote Plugin work with page caching "
"plugins</a> </b></p>\n"
"                                           </b> You can modify the <i>Quote "
"Request</i> page by modifying the \"rfq-cart.php\"\n"
"                                            template in \"plugins/woo-rfq-"
"for-woocommerce/woocommerce/woo-rfq/rfq-cart.php\".\n"
"                                           Create the \"woo-rfq\" folder "
"under \"your_child_theme/woocommerce\" and  Copy the \"rfq-cart.php\" file "
"to the \"woo-rfq\" folder \n"
"                                           under the WooCommerce directory "
"in your child theme directory and modify it. \n"
"                                           <b>You can read more <a "
"href=\"https://neahplugins.com/how-to-customize-the-quote-request-page/\" "
"target=\"_blank\" >\n"
"                                           How to customize the quote "
"request page</a></b>  <br /><br />\n"
"                                           You can also use the short code "
"<b>[gpls_woo_rfq_get_cart_sc]</b>  in your own page.</p>                     "
"                      \n"
"                                             "
msgstr ""

#: includes/classes/admin/settings/gpls_woo_rfq_settings.php:960
msgid ""
